---
// Go's map: a directory indexed by the top bits of the hash, pointing at
// independent Swiss tables of at most 1024 slots. One table splitting into two.
---

<figure class="go-dir">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 560 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="go-dir-title">
    <title id="go-dir-title">
      A hash's top bits index a directory of four entries. Entries 0 and 1 point at one shared table; entries 2 and
      3 point at separate tables. The shared table has filled up and is splitting into two.
    </title>
    <text class="label" x="0" y="18">hash</text>
    <rect class="box" x="0" y="26" width="150" height="26" rx="3" />
    <rect class="hi" x="1" y="27" width="34" height="24" rx="2" />
    <text class="mono" x="18" y="44" text-anchor="middle">10</text>
    <text class="mono muted" x="92" y="44" text-anchor="middle">…h1…  h2</text>
    <text class="label" x="0" y="80">top bits pick a directory entry</text>

    <text class="label" x="220" y="18">directory</text>
    {
      [0, 1, 2, 3].map((i) => (
        <>
          <rect class="box" x="220" y={26 + i * 34} width="60" height="28" rx="3" />
          <text class="mono" x="250" y={45 + i * 34} text-anchor="middle">
            {i.toString(2).padStart(2, '0')}
          </text>
        </>
      ))
    }
    <path class="arrow" d="M36 52 L220 40" />
    <path class="arrow" d="M150 39 L220 39" />

    <text class="label" x="340" y="18">tables, ≤ 1024 slots each</text>
    <rect class="box" x="340" y="26" width="200" height="56" rx="3" />
    <text class="mono" x="440" y="50" text-anchor="middle">table A (full)</text>
    <text class="mono muted" x="440" y="70" text-anchor="middle">entries 00 and 01 share it</text>
    <path class="arrow" d="M280 40 L340 45" />
    <path class="arrow" d="M280 74 L340 62" />

    <rect class="box" x="340" y="96" width="200" height="30" rx="3" />
    <text class="mono" x="440" y="115" text-anchor="middle">table B</text>
    <path class="arrow" d="M280 108 L340 111" />
    <rect class="box" x="340" y="136" width="200" height="30" rx="3" />
    <text class="mono" x="440" y="155" text-anchor="middle">table C</text>
    <path class="arrow" d="M280 142 L340 151" />

    <text class="label" x="340" y="196">A splits: entry 00 → A′, entry 01 → A″</text>
    <rect class="box accent" x="340" y="204" width="96" height="30" rx="3" />
    <text class="mono" x="388" y="223" text-anchor="middle">A′</text>
    <rect class="box accent" x="444" y="204" width="96" height="30" rx="3" />
    <text class="mono" x="492" y="223" text-anchor="middle">A″</text>
    <path class="arrow accent" d="M400 82 L388 204" />
    <path class="arrow accent" d="M480 82 L492 204" />
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="demo-caption">
    Go 1.24's map. A hash's top bits select a directory entry; each entry points at a Swiss table of at most 1,024
    slots. When table A fills, only A is rebuilt, as two tables, and the two directory entries that shared it are
    pointed at the halves. The rest of the map is untouched, so the cost of any one insert is bounded.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .go-dir {
    margin: 2.25rem 0;
  }

  svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 36rem;
    height: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .box {
    fill: var(--surface);
    stroke: var(--rule);
  }

  .box.accent {
    stroke: var(--accent);
  }

  .hi {
    fill: var(--accent);
    fill-opacity: 0.25;
  }

  .label {
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--muted);
  }

  .mono {
    font-size: 12px;
    fill: var(--fg);
  }

  .muted {
    fill: var(--muted);
  }

  .arrow {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--muted);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
  }

  .arrow.accent {
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-dasharray: 3 3;
  }
</style>
